{"hw":"ἀστός","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἀστός</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἀστός</span>, <span class=\"lex-gram\">ὁ</span>, (<span class=\"lex-etym gk\">ἄστυ</span>) <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">townsman, citizen,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">11.242</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">13.192</span> </span>, etc.; dist. from <span class=\"gk\">πολίτης, ἀστός</span> being <b class=\"lex-tr\">one who has civil rights</b> only, <span class=\"gk\">πολίτης</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">one who has political rights</b> also, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Arist.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pol.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1278a34</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἀ. πικρὸς πολίταις</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Med.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">223</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οἱ ἀ.</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">the commons,</b> opp. <span class=\"gk\">οἱ ἀγαθοί,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">P.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.71</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Isoc.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.21</span> </span>; opp. <span class=\"gk\">ξένος,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">O.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.90</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.160</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.8</span> </span>; esp. at Athens, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Lys.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.17</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ap.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">30a</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Isoc.</span> </span> l.c., cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">817</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">13</span> </span>, etc.; opp. <span class=\"gk\">μέτοικος, ξένος,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">R.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">563a</span> </span>; in Egypt, <b class=\"lex-tr\">citizen of Alexandria</b> (cf. <span class=\"gk\">ἄστυ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">11.3</span> </span> ), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">PGnom.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">38</span> </span>, al. —Fem. <span class=\"gk\">ἀστή,</span> q. v., but <span class=\"gk\">Ἀστός</span> fem. as epith. of <span class=\"gk\">Κόρη,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">12(5).225</span> </span> (Paros, <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">v B. C.</span>). (<span class=\"gk\">ϝασστός</span> and <span class=\"gk\">ϝαστός,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">IG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9(1).333.14</span> </span> (<span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Locr.</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">v B. C.</span>), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9(2).1226</span> </span> (Phalanna, <span class=\"lex-cite-date\">v B.C.</span>).)</div></div>"}